    {
        "id": "75393121-a091-4e15-b3e5-28312be35953",
        "build_id": "5b1b24b7-c0b6-47b6-9c69-6d07afc500e7",
        "round_number": 5,
        "cash_earned": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-07-26T21:09:32.165116+00:00",
        "notes": "Round 5 we typically grab  [Keen Kunai](item_d5993121-8a5f-4c59-9145-19dc55265f48). The way [Foxy Fireworks](item_d29ac7bb-d84c-44d7-8944-24c9b668b657) works, is as long as you are above 12/15 ammo, your kunai are explosive. So if you hit a headshot and reload back to 12+ ammo with  [Keen Kunai](item_d5993121-8a5f-4c59-9145-19dc55265f48), you can continue activating  [Foxy Fireworks](item_d29ac7bb-d84c-44d7-8944-24c9b668b657) without reloading! AND it has CD reduction allowing us to farm more suzus (with overhealth) and TPs, which all allow us to activate  [Ry\u014dta\u2019s Reloader](item_5cabe555-3845-49fa-9941-71b870c2c164) again. Very synergysitic! So go for headshots (also farms burst damage).\n\nFor items, I like  [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) soley for the extra CD reduction. But there are many good optiosn including  [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) and  [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f).\n\nAlso, if you don't feel like you can hit heads or just need some extra healing,  [Clone Conjuration](item_6c9f6be1-ab29-4f46-af24-34e4835f9af3) isn't a terrible choice either.",
